          "settings": {
            "title": "Diamond Carat",
            "use_h1": false
          }
        },
        "text_izVACg": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Carat is the measure used to describe a diamond’s weight, and one of the defining factors in its perceived presence. While it is often associated with scale, carat is a technical measure of weight rather than visible size alone.</p><p>A diamond’s appearance is always shaped by more than weight in isolation. The way it has been cut, proportioned and finished plays a central role in how beautifully it presents, which is why the most compelling diamonds are those whose presence feels balanced, refined and harmonious.</p>",
            "enlarge_text": false
          }
        },
        "button_UGWdG9": {
          "type": "button",
          "settings": {
            "button_label": "Learn More",
            "button_link": "https://williamedouard.com/pages/diamond-carat",
            "button_style": "secondary"
          }
        }
      },
