          "settings": {
            "title": "Diamond Colour",
            "use_h1": false
          }
        },
        "text_WFiXCh": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>White diamonds are graded on a scale from D, entirely colourless, through to Z, where warmer tones become increasingly visible. The rarest diamonds sit within the D to F range, where the absence of colour allows light to pass through the stone with exceptional purity.</p><p>Differences between neighbouring grades are often imperceptible to the untrained eye, yet they remain significant in rarity and value. Our collection is drawn predominantly from the D to G range.</p>",
            "enlarge_text": false
          }
        },
        "button_98wGPB": {
          "type": "button",
          "settings": {
            "button_label": "Learn More",
            "button_link": "https://williamedouard.com/pages/diamond-colour",
